+---
+id: task-002-implement-rfc-6902-json-patch-applypatch
+type: task
+title: "Implement RFC 6902 JSON Patch applyPatch"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Implement RFC 6902 JSON Patch applyPatch
+
+## Request
+
+Export `applyPatch(document, patch)` from `src/index.ts`: apply a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) with its six
+operations (add, remove, replace, move, copy, test), return the result as a new value without
+mutating the input, throw when the patch is invalid or an operation fails.
+
+## Done
+
+- `src/json-patch.ts`: `applyPatch`, `JsonPatchError`, and the `JsonPatch`/`JsonPatchOperation` types,
+  with no runtime dependency.
+- `src/json-pointer.ts`: the JSON Pointer code, moved from `src/index.ts` unchanged except for two
+  internal helpers (`resolveTokens`, `isArrayIndex`) used by JSON Patch. `src/index.ts` now re-exports
+  both modules; the public pointer API is unchanged.
+- `test/apply-patch.test.ts` (`npm test`), written first and seen failing: the examples of RFC 6902
+  appendix A (except A.13, a duplicate member that a JavaScript object cannot hold), each operation's
+  happy and error paths, `-` and index rules, root targets, `move` into a child, JSON equality for
+  `test`, malformed patches and operations, error `index`/`operation`/`cause`, `__proto__` safety,
+  and non-mutation of document and patch (also on failure). 57 tests pass, pointer tests included.
+- `README.md`: JSON Patch usage and error behaviour.
+- Decision: dl-003 (atomic copy-on-apply semantics and error reporting).
+
+## Notes
+
+- TypeScript is not installed in the repository, so `tsc` type-checking was not run; the tests run the
+  source through Node's type stripping.
+- No coverage threshold is declared in the project, so coverage was not measured.
